  <a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
  <site-header></site-header>
  <main class="page" id="main">
    <section class="hero flow">
      <card-note><p slot="text">Ceramics studio · Portfolio · 2025</p></card-note>
      <h1>Harbour Lane Pottery</h1>
      <p class="lead">A quiet portfolio for a working potter, with large photographs and a dates page for kiln openings.</p>
    </section>
    <section class="prose flow">
      <h2>The brief</h2>
      <p>The studio sold most of its work at kiln openings, but news of the dates travelled by word of mouth and a mailing list kept in a notebook. The potter wanted somewhere calm to show finished pieces without running an online shop.</p>
      <h2>What we built</h2>
      <p>A portfolio of large photographs with short captions, grouped by glaze, and a dates page that lists the next openings with directions to the studio. Adding a date is one line of text.</p>
      <h2>Since launch</h2>
      <p>Openings are now announced a month ahead, and the potter adds new pieces after each firing without asking us.</p>
      <p><a href="/#work">Back to all work</a></p>
    </section>
    <section-contact>
      <h2 slot="title">Need something similar?</h2>
      <p slot="body" class="body">Tell us what your site needs to do and we will reply within a few days.</p>
      <a slot="action" href="/about/#contact">Start a project</a>
    </section-contact>
  </main>
  <site-footer></site-footer>
